  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1050 AM MDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nThe main storm track is well to our north, which is a bit unusual\nfor October, but there are a few features to note in for the\nforecast. First is a NW-SE orientated ridge that runs across\nCentral/Southern CA into Northern Baja and Sonora into the rest of\nMexico, placing us within NW flow aloft. There is also a very weak\ndisturbance over CO. Then, you of course have Isaias (not going to\nbe a direct player in our weather), Rachel, and Twenty-E. \n\nThe weak disturbance over CO will have some influence on our\nweather today and tomorrow. It will mainly be in the form of\nisolated showers or thunderstorms. For this afternoon, chances\nwill mainly be limited to the Gila with storms struggling to make\ninto the lowlands. The NAM Nest and HRRR show weak showers forming\nover mainly Hudspeth toward daybreak tomorrow morning, and then we\nreturn to isolated showers/storms over mainly the mountains with\none or two cells making it into the lowlands tomorrow. Any shower\nor storm during the afternoon could produce some gusty outflow \nwinds. Temperatures will be a few degrees above normal.\n\nAs we go into Friday and into the weekend, we find ourselves in a\nsomewhat nondescript pattern. Both the GFS and Euro show a weak \ns/w cross over NM Friday, but neither model produce any \nprecip/QPF. We then fill in with a ridge on Saturday with a \nsubtropical tap developing ahead of a closed low off the Baja \nCoast (partially the remnants of Rachel). This pattern will bring \nsome rain chances to the Gila and areas adjacent to the Arizona \nborder. \n\nGoing into next week, the trough-Rachel hybrid (not technically\nscientifically correct wording, but it works) will begin lifting\ninto the CONUS, spreading considerable moisture northward. For\nnow, it looks like the focus will be over AZ, possibly clipping\nfar west NM. The wild card, just beyond the forecast, is what will\nbecome of now TD Twenty-E. The 00Z ECMWF and 6z GFS bring its\nremnants directly to us. The 12z GFS is falling in line with the\n6z run, more or less. Nevertheless, the ensemble members are not\nfavoring this solution, so at this point, there is low confidence\nin this scenario. It is definitely something that will need to be\nwatched though!",
